hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1235","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb bin Muslim told us, my uncle told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told me Allah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal, that his father Abdullah bin Al-Harith said: I asked and was keen to find someone who would tell me that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the morning prayer, but I did not find anyone to tell me about that except Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came after daylight on the day of the conquest and ordered a garment to be covered over and he bathed, then he got up and kneeled eight times. Rakats. I do not know whether his standing in them was longer, or his bowing or prostration, all of that is similar. She said: I did not see him praising her before or after."
